@startuml gameplay-activity
title Play a Domino Match — activity
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
start
:Use the already full, configured match;
note right
  Precondition: authenticated participants;
  2 or 3 individual players (draw), or
  4 players in fixed opposing-seat teams (block).
  Joining and inviting are separate use cases.
end note
:Shuffle the 28 unique double-six tiles;\ndeal 7 tiles to each participant;
if (4 participants?) then (yes)
  :No boneyard; holder of 6|6 opens with 6|6;
else (2 or 3)
  :Keep undealt tiles in the boneyard;\nhighest dealt double opens with that double;
  note right
    If no double was dealt: highest total pips
    opens; break ties by highest end.
  end note
endif
:Apply opening placement;\nadvance to next seat; reset consecutive passes;
:Display board, own hand and active seat;
while (Match still active?) is (yes)
  :Receive an action from any participant;\nvalidate turn and requested action;
  note right
    Place: owned tile matches selected end.
    Draw: individual variant, no legal placement,
    and stock remains.
    Pass: no legal placement and no stock.
  end note
  if (Action valid?) then (no)
    :Explain rejection;\nleave board, hands, turn and passes unchanged;
  else (yes)
    if (Draw?) then (yes)
      repeat
        :Draw one tile into active player's hand;
      repeat while (No legal tile and stock remains?) is (yes) not (no)
      :Show updated hand and stock count;\nkeep same turn for placement or pass;
    else (place or pass)
      if (Placement?) then (yes)
        :Place tile; remove it from hand;\nreset consecutive passes;
        if (Hand now empty?) then (yes)
          :End match immediately;\nplayer wins (2/3) or team wins (4);
        else (no)
          :Advance to next seat;
        endif
      else (pass)
        :Record pass;
        if (All participants passed consecutively?) then (yes)
          :End blocked match;\nlowest personal pips (2/3) or team pips (4) wins;\nequal lowest totals tie;
        else (no)
          :Advance to next seat;
        endif
      endif
    endif
    :Make accepted state available to all participants;\nshow each player only their own hand;
  endif
endwhile (no)
:Display winner or tie and end reason;\nshow pip totals for a blocked result;
stop
note right
  Client success requires a confirmed server response.
  Missing delivery is not a server rejection or rollback.
  Disconnect/recovery behavior remains unresolved.
end note
@enduml
